      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This behavior appears to be caused by drone self-leveling. I have taken a video\n\nI think the strategy to take to solve the problem is either\n\n* Automatically adjust the target y-coordinate for self-leveling according to the amount of change in the y-coordinate before and after the call to `VRCDroneApi.TeleportTo()` (we may need to switch the behavior with a new argument of `TeleportTo()`)\n\n* Expose methods like `VRCDroneApi.TryGetLevelY()` / `.SetLevelY()`.\n\nこの振る舞いはドローンのセルフレベリングによって起きているように見えます。動画を撮影しました\n\n問題を解消するために取るべき戦略は以下のどちらかだと考えます\n\n* セルフレベリングのターゲットy座標を、 `VRCDroneApi.TeleportTo()` の呼び出し前後でY座標の変化量に応じて自動で調節する（ `TeleportTo()` の引数で挙動を切り替える必要があるかもしれません）\n\n* `VRCDroneApi.TryGetLevelY()` / `.SetLevelY()` のようなメソッドを公開する",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-04-07T06:27:00.978Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I've been fiddling around with new drone API since it is public, but I found out sometimes it is quirky when calling `VRCDroneApi.TeleportTo()` with Udon(sharp).\n\nWhatever what coordinate you want to teleport the drone to, the drone will always drift back to the same y-level it was.\n\nI don't know if this should consider a SDK bug or drone bug.",
